# 詞: 銀包

1. 我唔小心將銀包遺留喺茶餐廳，嚇到一身冷汗。 (I accidentally left my wallet at the cha chaan teng and was scared stiff.)
2. 你個銀包好舊呀，係咪該換新嘅啦？ (Your wallet looks really old. Is it time to get a new one?)
3. 佢成日話自己冇錢，但係個銀包厚過磚頭。 (He always says he has no money, but his wallet is thicker than a brick.)
4. 小心啲啦，唔好將銀包放喺後袋，容易被人扒走。 (Be careful, don't put your wallet in your back pocket; it's easy for pickpockets to steal it.)
5. 我哋去旅行之前，記得檢查下銀包入面有冇帶夠現金。 (Before we go on our trip, remember to check if there's enough cash in your wallet.)
6. 佢個銀包上面印住佢鍾意嘅卡通人物，好可愛。 (There's a cartoon character he likes printed on his wallet; it's so cute.)
7. 我個銀包壞咗，拉鏈打唔開，要即刻去修。 (My wallet is broken; the zipper won't open, so I need to get it fixed immediately.)
8. 你唔好成日將銀包攞出嚟擺喺枱面，唔安全。 (Don't keep taking your wallet out and placing it on the table; it's not safe.)
9. 佢送咗個新銀包畀我，話祝我財源廣進。 (He gave me a new wallet, saying he wished me abundant wealth.)
10. 我搵唔到我個銀包，心入面好慌張，以為被人偷咗。 (I can't find my wallet; I'm really panicked inside, thinking it might have been stolen.) [end of text]


